From dd4b72d3dbc6f54428bbf369e2861a0376297a32 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dfattal <dfattal@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 25 Aug 2026 22:48:56 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 116/117] inline-3d(runtime#625): read the runtime's
 weaved-output RING (spec v10)

The runtime weaves into ONE texture that we read while it is already weaving the
next frame into it -- xrWeaveSubmitDXR performs the weave for v+1 inside the very
call we then read a v-or-earlier fence value from, so the producer is
structurally a frame ahead at read time. The woven image is view-interlaced, so a
torn read is not a displaced edge but a band where BOTH eyes get the wrong view:
a flash.

Spec v10 lets the runtime rotate between N separate woven textures instead, and
tells us which one each frame landed in. Opt in by chaining XrWeaveRingRequestDXR
on the submit and reading the reported index back from XrWeaveOutputSliceDXR.

N SEPARATE textures rather than array slices of one: we import the woven output
through the SharedImage layer, and `CreateSharedImage(mailbox, si_info,
GpuMemoryBufferHandle(DXGIHandle))` takes a handle plus a 2D size with nowhere to
name a slice. An array would at best expose slice 0. N plain 2D textures import
unchanged, so this needs no shared-image-layer surgery.

- weave_client: chain the request (gated on the runtime's reported spec version,
  same discipline as the v8 flat-regions chain -- an older runtime must not be
  handed a struct type it has never heard of), and carry index/count/handles out.
- mojom + weaver_impl: |extra_outputs| carries outputs 1..N-1; output 0 IS
  |woven|, so it is not sent twice (two handles to one texture would both need
  closing). Non-empty only on the frames |woven| is.
- weave_gpu: same carry-forward rule as |woven| for a dropped reply, and
  CloseResultHandles closes the extras -- missing that leaks one NT handle per
  extra output on every dropped reply.
- viz: import the whole ring alongside the existing mailbox and sample the one
  the runtime names. Index 0 IS the legacy mailbox, so a pre-v10 runtime (index 0
  of 1, no extras) walks exactly the path it walks today.

Vendored XR_DXR_weave.h synced from the runtime at spec v10.
